.TH geectl-build-rebuild-package 1  "geectl-build-rebuild-package 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-build\-rebuild\-package \- Rebuild a package: rerun a build without touching the sources. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the rebuild
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl build rebuild\-package\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> <\fIREPOSITORY\fR> <\fIARCH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rebuild a package: rerun a build without touching the sources. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the rebuild
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package is in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package to rebuild
.TP
<\fIREPOSITORY\fR>
The repository the package builds in
.TP
<\fIARCH\fR>
The architecture the package builds for
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
